    <meta name="description" content="What is gravitational force?" />
    
</svelte:head>
<article>
    <h1>{$selectedSection}</h1>
    <section>
        <p>
            Objects that have mass exert gravitational force on each other. It is an attractive force. If {`\\(m, M\\)`} are masses of two particles, then the magnitude of force due to gravitation is given by {`\\[F = \\frac{GMm}{r^2}\\]`} where {`\\(r\\)`} is the distance between the two particles and {`\\(G = 6.67\\times 10^{-11}~Nm^2/kg^2\\)`} is known as the Gravitational constant. The direction of the force {`\\(F\\)`} is along the line joining the particles. If there are more than two particles, then each particle exerts gravitational force on other particle. In the figure below, there are 5 particles. Each one experiences gravitational force due to the other 4. These forces are pairwise equal in magnitude, but opposite in direction. For example, {`\\[\\vec{F}_{15} = -\\vec{F}_{51}\\]`}
        </p>
