    <section>
        <h2>Gravitational force is really small</h2>
        <p>If two bodies each of mass 1 kg are kept next to each other at a distance of 1 m, then the force due to gravity between them will be {`\\(F = \\dfrac{6.7\\times 10^{-11}\\times 1 \\times 1}{1^2}=6.7\\times 10^{-11}N\\)`} That is why, in most practical situations, we ignore force due to gravity between object except the one exerted by the Earth (which is significant). </p>
    </section>
